# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Signing credentials TEMPLATE  ·  copy to keystore/keystore.properties
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# THIS TREE SHIPS ITS KEY. keystore/vega-release-v5.jks and its password are in
# keystore/README-KEYSTORE.md, because the whole tree is delivered privately to
# its owner and losing the key would force another uninstall/reinstall cycle on
# every future release. Nothing needs to be filled in here to build.
#
# This file stays as a template for the OTHER arrangement — a published source
# tree whose release key is held privately, so an APK not signed with that exact
# key cannot pose as an update:
#   1. Keep the .jks somewhere OUTSIDE this repo, e.g. ~/keys/vega-release-v5.jks
#   2. cp keystore/keystore.properties.example  keystore/keystore.properties
#   3. Fill in the values below.  keystore/keystore.properties is git-ignored,
#      so the secret never lands in version control.
#
# build.gradle.kts and ./mkapk.sh both read these (env vars / -P flags win over
# this file). For CI, do NOT use this file — add repository secrets instead
# (VEPRO_KEYSTORE_BASE64, VEPRO_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD, VEPRO_KEY_ALIAS); see SIGNING.md.
#
# NEVER commit a filled-in copy of this file or the .jks itself.

storeFile=/absolute/path/OUTSIDE/this/repo/vega-release-v5.jks
storeType=PKCS12
storePassword=CHANGE_ME
keyAlias=vega
keyPassword=CHANGE_ME
